# docs/references.title-allow — exceptions for the TITLE cross-check.
#
# `QAtlasHub/doiget-citation-check` compares each entry's title against the one its DOI
# resolves to. That catches a mistyped DOI that lands on somebody else's real paper —
# which the resolution gate cannot, since the wrong DOI resolves fine. Measured on this
# bibliography: 2 of 18 sampled DOIs have a resolving neighbour one digit away.
#
# Kept SEPARATE from references.allow so that exempting an entry here does not also exempt
# it from the resolution gate.
#
# Only entries the gate actually stops belong here. A resolved title that is merely SHORTER
# than the entry's is reported and never gated, so publisher truncation needs no exemption.

Haldane1988   # Crossref truncates mid-word, at "…chain with 1/" — not a prefix of a word
Korringa1950  # the registered title itself misspells it, "resonnance"
